# JOB 1 #
position1=System Analyst
company1=AMDOCS Inc
date1=April 2018 - Present
jobDetails1=Led end-to-end analysis, design, development, integration, and support of large-scale telecom billing systems, ensuring high availability, accuracy, and regulatory compliance across mission-critical platforms.;Designed and implemented end-to-end system integrations between billing platforms and multiple upstream/downstream systems including CRM, order management, mediation, OSS, reporting systems, enabling seamless data flow and operational efficiency.;Acted as solution architect and technical lead for complex billing enhancements, troubleshooting critical production issues, performing root cause analysis, and driving long-term system stability and performance improvements.;Delivered full SDLC ownership: requirements gathering, solution design, development, testing, production deployment, and post-go-live support.;Played a key role in legacy system transformation, system migrations, data transformation, and architecture redesign for next-generation systems.;Leveraged AI-powered tools across the entire SDLC to accelerate: Business requirement analysis, Code generation and refactoring, Debugging and root cause analysis, Documentation and knowledge base creation. Increased development and delivery efficiency by adopting AI-driven tools for overall solution quality.;Served as technical mentor and doing knowledge transfer both legacy applications and newly developed tools to rapidly upskill team members.;Collaborated closely with product owners, architects, QA teams, DevOps and business analysts to deliver high-impact solutions aligned with business objectives.;Provided L2/L3 production support, handling high-severity incidents and performance degradation issues while maintaining strict SLA compliance.;Built custom internal tools and utilities for developers and testers to: Automate repetitive development and testing tasks, Simplify environment setup and data preparation, Accelerate debugging, validation, and testing, Improve developer productivity and test coverage.;Advising the team on optimized methods for preparing and managing SQL scripts during technical/script reviews to improve overall performance & efficiency.

# JOB 2 #
position2=Software Engineer
company2=PLDT
date2=March 2011 - April 2018
jobDetails2=Performed end‑to‑end configuration of complex Billing System components, including Products, Usage, Journals, Extended Data, and Parameter configurations, ensuring alignment with business and operational requirements.;Analyzed Business Requirement Specifications (BRS) and translated them into scalable, efficient technical solutions that support billing and customer management processes.;Developed and optimized Shell scripts and PL/SQL programs, executing thorough unit testing to validate functionality before turnover to QA/testing teams.;Provided comprehensive testing support across the SDLC, including System Acceptance Testing (SAT), Integration Acceptance Testing (IAT), User Acceptance Testing (UAT), and Production Integration Testing (PIT).;Delivered Level 3 support for Billing and BSS platforms by performing root-cause analysis, resolving production issues, and implementing permanent corrective actions.;Executed scripts required for audit, compliance, and operational reporting, ensuring data integrity and accurate traceability.;Performed report extractions and data analysis to support business operations, performance tracking, and system validation activities.
